| Runtime/provider acceptance | Complete the four categories on the supported matrix; resolve reference/runtime and provider acceptance blockers | Full-port lead; full inventory and owner allocation remain incomplete |
| Migration, recovery, privacy and measurement | Exercise signed-in migration, files/accounts/rules/mods, rollback/recovery, publication provenance and cold/warm measurements | Required by the contract; no completed combined acceptance receipt observed |

The estimate assumes these areas can proceed in parallel, current corrections
remain useful, and independent verification does not uncover a broader missing
subsystem. Missing coverage, unavailable native/reference fixtures, failed
independent review or a newly discovered subsystem can extend the range.
Successful local tests alone do not shorten it. A defensible narrower forecast
requires a reconciled remaining-case inventory, owner estimates and an observed
repair/verification rate; these are engineering work, not operator questions.

